# UI rules

- Reuse existing components under `components/` and shadcn/ui primitives before creating new ones.
- Do not redesign pages, layouts, or visual language unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve responsive behavior already present in the app.
- Follow existing Tailwind and design-system patterns; do not introduce a new UI library without justification.
- Prefer extending `JobBoard`, sidebar, forms, and dialogs already in the repo over parallel implementations.
- Keep client components (`"use client"`) for interactive UI; keep data fetching and mutations aligned with existing API routes.
- Treat external HTML (job descriptions) as untrusted: sanitize or convert before rendering.
- Do not place unrelated marketing or landing redesign work into authenticated app routes.
